.TH SLEEP "1" "July 2026" "PiggyOS" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
sleep \- do nothing for a specified amount of time

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sleep
\fI\,NUMBER\/\fR[\fI\,UNIT\/\fR]...

.SH DESCRIPTION

.PP
Pause for NUMBER seconds, where NUMBER is an integer or floating\-point value.
UNIT may be 's', 'm', 'h', or 'd', for seconds, minutes, hours, or days respectively.
With multiple arguments, pause for the sum of the their values.

.SH OPTIONS
None.

